{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Shimon and Levi, brothers.</b> It is known that they were brothers. But by way of the plain sense (peshat), they became brothered as one in instruments of violence in the affair of Shechem. And the phrase מכרותיהם means 'their feasts' — from the root of (Job 40:30) ״יכרו עליו חברים״. And the meaning of כלי חמס is 'weapons of sustenance' — they live and are nourished by them. And he explains here that they committed violence when they killed the people of Shechem, who had not sinned against them but had entered into a covenant and been circumcised, and it was not fitting to do so. Therefore he excuses himself, for he was not in their counsel — this is what he said: 'Into their council let my soul not come.'" "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'Shimon and Levi, brothers' — brothers in the matter of Dinah, but not brothers in the matter of Yosef. Brothers in the matter of Dinah, as it is said (Genesis 34:25) 'the brothers of Dinah'; but not brothers in the matter of Yosef, for they sold him. You may know this: Reuven, Shimon, Levi, and Yehudah were the eldest. Reuven — it is written (Genesis 37:22) 'in order to save him.' Yehudah — it is written (ibid.) 'What gain is there if we kill.' From this you learn that Shimon and Levi sold him. Therefore when they went down to Egypt, he took none of them but Shimon alone — thus far in Bereshit Rabbah." "<b>Instruments of violence, their feasts.</b> Instruments that are in their hands, plundered and stolen, are from Esav, as it is said (Obadiah): ״מחמס אחיך יעקב תכסה בושה״." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> 'Shimon and Levi, brothers.' I have already written that there is in them an allusion to the six extremities together with what is above them, for all is one and unified one with the other, and the allusion to this is surely: 'Shimon and Levi, brothers.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {1 "Printed citation reads (שם) 'ibid.'; the prooftext מה בצע כי נהרוג appears at Genesis 37:26, not 37:22; (שם) may refer loosely to the same chapter."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:28.054501255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}